<Layout title="Research" description="Research by Binh Minh Tran in graph learning, multimodal biomedical AI, computational RNA biology, and individualised probability modelling after high-risk NIPT.">
  <section class="page-header container"><p class="academic-kicker">Research overview</p><h1>Research</h1><p class="page-lead">I build machine learning methods that connect different views of biological systems, from RNA networks and tissue microenvironments to patient outcomes.</p></section>
  <section class="container research-overview" id="current"><div class="research-direction"><p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span> Current focus · ANU</p><h2>Computational RNA biology</h2><p>I’m undertaking preliminary research with Professor Eduardo Eyras at the Centre for Computational Biomedical Sciences, John Curtin School of Medical Research, Australian National University.</p><p>The central question: how can AI/ML help interpret variants that affect RNA modifications such as m6A, pseudouridine, and m5C, while distinguishing predicted modification changes from disease-relevant functional effects?</p><div class="tag-row"><span>Computational RNA biology</span><span>Variant interpretation</span><span>RNA modifications</span></div><p class="small-note">Visiting Researcher since October 2026 · Early-stage research</p></div><aside class="research-principles"><p class="eyebrow">How I approach research</p><ol><li><span>01</span><div><h3>Represent the structure</h3><p>Use graphs to model relationships across cells, molecules, and biological networks.</p></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><h3>Connect the modalities</h3><p>Bring molecular, imaging, and clinical information into a shared learning framework.</p></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><h3>Evaluate carefully</h3><p>Use patient-level validation, external cohorts, and interpretable analyses.</p></div></li></ol></aside></section>
  <section class="section container"><div class="section-heading section-heading-inline"><div><h2>Research projects</h2></div><span class="small-note">2024 — 2027 · Including planned work</span></div><div class="project-grid">{projects.map(project=><ProjectCard project={project} />)}</div></section>
</Layout>
